  "segments": [
    {
      "id": "0",
      "text": "Tables"
    },
    {
      "id": "1",
      "text": "Tables are supported with standard markup. Here's a typical table with a\nheading row, several regular rows, and a row marked up as {code1}&#x3C;tr class=\"alt\">{/code1},\nwhich produces a darker background that can be used as an alternate header."
    },
    {
      "id": "2",
      "text": "One"
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
      "text": "Two"
    },
    {
      "id": "4",
      "text": "Three"
    },
    {
      "id": "5",
      "text": "1.0"
    },
    {
      "id": "6",
      "text": "2.0"
    },
    {
      "id": "7",
      "text": "3.0"
    },
    {
      "id": "8",
      "text": "1.1"
    },
    {
      "id": "9",
      "text": "2.1"
    },
    {
      "id": "10",
      "text": "3.1"
    },
    {
      "id": "11",
      "text": "Here come some numbers that end in .2!"
    },
    {
      "id": "12",
      "text": "1.2"
    },
    {
      "id": "13",
      "text": "2.2"
    },
    {
      "id": "14",
      "text": "3.2"
    },
    {
      "id": "15",
      "text": "{code1}&#x3C;table>\n  &#x3C;tr>&#x3C;th>One&#x3C;/th>&#x3C;th>Two&#x3C;/th>&#x3C;th>Three&#x3C;/th>&#x3C;/tr>\n  &#x3C;tr>&#x3C;td>1.0&#x3C;/td>&#x3C;td>2.0&#x3C;/td>&#x3C;td>3.0&#x3C;/td>&#x3C;/tr>\n  &#x3C;tr>&#x3C;td>1.1&#x3C;/td>&#x3C;td>2.1&#x3C;/td>&#x3C;td>3.1&#x3C;/td>&#x3C;/tr>\n  &#x3C;tr class=\"alt\">&#x3C;td colspan=\"3\">Here come some numbers that end in .2!&#x3C;/td>&#x3C;/tr>\n  &#x3C;tr>&#x3C;td>1.2&#x3C;/td>&#x3C;td>2.2&#x3C;/td>&#x3C;td>3.2&#x3C;/td>&#x3C;/tr>\n&#x3C;/table>\n{/code1}"
    },
    {
      "id": "16",
      "text": "Responsive tables"
    },
    {
      "id": "17",
      "text": "To make a table responsive, add the {code1}responsive{/code1} class to the table."
    },
    {
      "id": "18",
      "text": "Parameters"
    },
    {
      "id": "19",
      "text": "value"
    },
    {
      "id": "20",
      "text": "String"
    },
    {
      "id": "21",
      "text": " the choice's value, which respondents see as a label when viewing the form"
    },
    {
      "id": "22",
      "text": "navigationType"
    },
    {
      "id": "23",
      "text": "PageNavigationType"
    },
    {
      "id": "24",
      "text": " the choice's navigation type"
    },
    {
      "id": "25",
      "text": "There must be "
    },
    {
      "id": "26",
      "text": "only two columns"
    },
    {
      "id": "27",
      "text": " in the table: the first column for the things being defined (the key), and the second column for all information about that key, in multiple lines if necessary. This two-column restriction means that responsive tables cannot be used for truly two-dimensional tabular data, checkmark-based feature comparison, but they are well suited for reference information (or anything other data that could reasonably be expressed by a definition list instead of a table)."
    },
    {
      "id": "28",
      "text": "If there are multiple lines of information about the key — say, a type and a description — wrap each line in "
    },
    {
      "id": "29",
      "text": "<p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "30",
      "text": " to force line breaks (instead of "
    },
    {
      "id": "31",
      "text": "<br>"
    },
    {
      "id": "32",
      "text": ")."
    },
    {
      "id": "33",
      "text": "There must be only one cell in the header row. Use "
    },
    {
      "id": "34",
      "text": "<th colspan=\"2\">"
    },
    {
      "id": "35",
      "text": " to force it to span both columns. To remind you of this behavior, we automatically hides any "
    },
    {
      "id": "36",
      "text": "<th>"
    },
    {
      "id": "37",
      "text": " after the first (which intentionally looks very broken)."
    },
    {
      "id": "38",
      "text": "{code1}&#x3C;table class=\"responsive\">\n  &#x3C;tbody>\n    &#x3C;tr>\n      &#x3C;th colspan=2>Parameters&#x3C;/th>\n    &#x3C;/tr>\n    &#x3C;tr>\n      &#x3C;td>\n        &#x3C;code>value&#x3C;/code>\n      &#x3C;/td>\n      &#x3C;td>\n        &#x3C;code>String&#x3C;/code>&#x3C;br>\n        the choice's value, which respondents see as a label when viewing the form\n      &#x3C;/td>\n    &#x3C;/tr>\n    &#x3C;tr>\n      &#x3C;td>\n        &#x3C;code>navigationType&#x3C;/code>\n      &#x3C;/td>\n      &#x3C;td>\n        &#x3C;code>\n          &#x3C;a href=\"#\">PageNavigationType&#x3C;/a>\n        &#x3C;/code>\n        &#x3C;br>the choice's navigation type\n      &#x3C;/td>\n    &#x3C;/tr>\n  &#x3C;/tbody>\n&#x3C;/table>\n{/code1}"
    },
    {
      "id": "39",
      "text": "Invisible tables"
    },
    {
      "id": "40",
